{"parentUuid":"e3109e13-71a9-465a-b4dd-ab21e23817d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"gen_01KTPZZRAPTEHW3QVHX4M8AS0Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The product page title now appears immediately on navigation.\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` awaited `getInventory()` at the top of the page component, and `getInventory` calls `connection()`, which defers rendering to request time. With `cacheComponents` enabled, that made the whole page dynamic — the title, which depends on no data, was blocked behind the server fetch on every navigation.\n\n**The fix:** I moved the inventory fetch into a child `Inventory` component and wrapped it in a `Suspense` boundary (app/product/page.tsx:19). The page component itself is now synchronous, so the title and layout are part of the prerendered static shell, and only the stock count and price stream in afterward (with a \"Loading inventory…\" fallback in the meantime).\n\nThe build confirms it — `/product` went from fully dynamic to Partial Prerender:\n\n```\n└ ◐ /product\n◐  (Partial Prerender)  prerendered as static HTML with dynamic server-streamed content\n```\n\nNavigating from home now paints the title instantly from the static shell while the inventory data streams in."}],"model":"claude-fable-5","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5075,"cache_read_input_tokens":29912,"output_tokens":453,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5075},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"13af4dfb-9aaa-4a0e-a481-0f25370b5275","timestamp":"2026-06-09T20:08:16.640Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/workspace","sessionId":"64b74f07-7e2c-4cec-be9f-12d008be9883","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"master"}
